<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>X3Code.Infrastructure</PackageId>
    <Product>X3Code.Infrastructure</Product>
    <Title>X3-Code Infrastructure</Title>
    <Description>Contains the unit of work repository pattern</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>10.0.0: New version scheme - the major now tracks the .NET generation the package is built for (net10.0), the minor carries features and breaking changes, the patch carries fixes. All X3Code packages move to 10.0.0 together.
The package now ships its XML documentation, so consumers get IntelliSense. Added an MIT license expression, a README and a symbol package (snupkg) with SourceLink.
Fixed malformed documentation tags on IRepository and GenericRepository, and an unescaped comparison in the DecimalExtension docs.
Entity Framework Core 10.0.3 -> 10.0.11, Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.1.4 -> 6.1.6.
All asynchronous methods on IRepository/GenericRepository now take a CancellationToken and pass it down into Entity Framework. The parameter is optional, so existing call sites keep compiling.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Geteilte Quelldatei, bewusst statt eines ProjectReference. Siehe CLAUDE.md. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\X3Code.Utils\Extensions\DataTableExtension.cs">
      <Link>Extensions\DataTableExtension.cs</Link>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
